{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And they took, etc. — which Moses commanded.</b> In saying <b>which Moses commanded</b>, it also intends Aaron himself, that he too took what he had been commanded; and this does not depart from the implication of the act of Israel, for even though the matters were said to them from Aaron's mouth, Aaron himself said them from Moses' mouth. And had the verse said ״which Aaron commanded,״ it would imply only the taking of Israel and not the taking of Aaron. Further, it may be that in saying <b>which Moses commanded</b> it intends that they did the thing solely by virtue of Moses' command, even though the promise recorded in the statement was not [yet] fulfilled."], :book :leviticus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:54:32.045207472Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}